                <pb facs="0832" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.16/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Chargé of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-12T20:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1920—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 13—3:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Hondurean Government has received an ultimatum from the Salvadorean
                    Government which arrived after the time of grace had passed and Hondurean
                    Minister Resident in Salvador also reports that General Leiva started to-day to
                    invade Honduras with arms supplied by the Salvadorean Government. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
